A: {name_b} is it true theres a dragon under avalon? someone said two heads | {name_b}, tell the one about the crystal cave
C: shh, let {name_b} talk. this is the xanxicar one | everybody quiet, avalon story
D: go ahead {name_b}, i always wondered whats under that isle | yes tell it, i have only seen the cave mouth
B: ok. there is a map of avalon older than any other. it marks something at the heart of the isle. no name on it
B: thats him. xanxicar. two heads, older than the map. the inconnu say even arawn wont go near him
B: a surveyor called caradoc laid the first college's stone right on the warm ground above him
B: and for three hundred years the college of stars sang over him on the longest night. the Quieting, they called it
?F: like a lullaby? for a dragon? | they sang a dragon to sleep every year
B: a lullaby or a ward, nobody is sure which. it worked either way
B: morgana sang it herself as a pupil. and that college is the first one she burned
~ 8
D: so who woke him? | and then he woke up i guess?
B: third night of the burning, dura'ek went down the stair. the guards who followed him came up as xanxicar's household
B: dura'ek came up with the dragon's two breaths. so xanxicar fights with his weight now. he rears and the cobbles crack
?E: yeah we noticed. 110 of us noticed | the stomp. dont remind me
B: sir garan lost five companies of forty at the cave mouth. five
B: the readers at caer gothwaite think he isnt even the power under avalon. just its keeper. lying on something worse
~ 25
F: lying on something worse. great | so what is he keeping
A: nobody knows. thats the part i like | {name_b} always stops right there

