A: {name_b} you there? tell the one about the dragon in malmohus | skald {name_b}! the gjalpinulva story, come on
C: quiet in the hall, {name_b} is telling the frost dragon | shh, all of you. malmohus story
?E: oh good, the wolf's daughter again | i can recite this one by now
D: tell it {name_b}, i only ever heard pieces | please {name_b}, i want the whole thing for once
B: ha. alright. ale down, ears open | fine. once, properly
B: the skalds say she is the fenris wolf's daughter. born before the gods finished his fetter
B: nobody agrees on the mother. jordheim says the giantess gjalp. the old women of aegir say iarnvidiur of the iron wood
B: she flew south over raumarik and skona and came down in the ruins of malmohus. and the cold went out from her like water
?F: is that why the ground is frozen there | so the frost in malmohus is HER
B: its her cloak. she wears the frost. outside her court no blow lands on her at all
B: she bred the drakulv there. yar was the firstborn. she ranked them like a court
B: then she called the varulv of skona to serve her. roared their envoys still while she named her terms
~ 8
D: and they agreed?? | did the wolves bend the knee?
B: king hresvelgr of varulvhamn told her no. and no werewolf has crossed into malmohus since
B: the svartalfar went to the ruins too. the first of them met her eyes and froze where they stood
B: the ones who lived founded the dragonbane of svarhamr. they have watched her ever since
B: hallbjorn of fort atla led the first eighty against her. found her bare only in her own hollow
?E: and that is still the only place she bleeds. ask me how i know
~ 25
F: remind me to never look her in the eye | the freezing part. ugh
C: good telling {name_b}. the fire feels warmer now

