B: so. tuscar was a smith long before he was a king
B: the rime giants say he was apprentice to the giant who built asgard's wall in one winter
B: you know that one. loki cheated the builder of his wage and thor's hammer paid him instead
?F: the builder got killed for doing the job? | wait the gods just didnt pay
B: they didnt pay. and when they came to settle it, the apprentice stole something from the forge
B: an oath-word of odin's. the one that sealed the bargain. he burned it into the haft of his hammer
B: thats why he calls on odin when hes hurt, and gets stronger. the god's own broken oath answers him
~ 8
D: is that true or just giants bragging? | do the skalds believe that?
B: jordheim's skalds say its a giant's boast. the iarn dwarves believe it. and dwarves know smiths
B: he made every weapon in tuscaran. the best axe of his life he made for kula. crossed the sea ice to give it to her
B: he tells every enemy the same thing. my queen carries the best weapon i ever made. mine is almost as good
?E: and then he hits you with almost as good | i have met almost as good. it hurt
B: but kill kula in front of him and he forgets the forge. he just screams for her
~ 25
