@topic tale_cuuldurach-the-glimmer-king
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_cuuldurach
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} are you about? tell the glimmer king story | {name_b}, the tale of cuuldurach, if you would
C: hush now, all. {name_b} tells the sheeroe hills one | quiet, friends, this is the glimmer king
?E: the one where the grass goes grey. again | i know how this one ends, the door stays open
D: oh please do {name_b} | go on {name_b}, i have never heard it start to finish
B: very well. gather in | once more then, and listen this time
B: the hills above the bog of cullen were only summer pasture. shepherds, sheep, nothing more
B: but they were always one of the realms of the otherworld too. unseen. with its own law and its own king
B: then one summer the sky tore over the ridge. a pass appeared that had not been there the day before
?F: a door just opened? in the hills? | the pass was not there before?
B: and through it came cuuldurach with a court of cold light. and the grass went grey behind him
B: the elven sage tyldifyl told the rangers plainly. sheeroe was always his. only the door is new
B: he is the only HE among the three dragons. and the only one who came as a king
~ 8
D: why did it open though? | does anyone know why that summer?
B: no one agrees. the druids of lough gur say the veil wore thin after the bargain broke in the cursed forest
B: he warns once, from the sky. he keeps a chamberlain. his heir maldahar rides the borders
B: conaing of howth took forty to his lair, the first to reach it. and found no blade would bite him once he left it
B: the druids named that the King's Law. a king may not be wounded on ground that is not his
?E: which is why we drag nobody anywhere. we fight him at home
~ 25
F: a king may not be wounded on ground not his. i like that | cold light. i can almost see it
A: thank you {name_b}. lovely as ever | beautifully told, {name_b}

